.Dd @PACKAGE_DATE@
.Dt GCLI-ATTACHMENTS 1
.Os @PACKAGE_STRING@
.Sh NAME
.Nm gcli\ attachments
.Nd Create, view or update Bugzilla attachments
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl i Ar attachment
.Ar actions...
.Nm
.Cm create
.Fl f Ar file
.Fl s Ar summary
.Fl i Ar bug-id
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl P
.Op Fl c Ar comment
.Op fl C Ar content-type
.Op Fl F Ar filename
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is used to manage Bugzilla attachments.
Attachments are referred to by unique IDs.
You can assoiate attachments with one or more bugs.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl i , -id
Execute actions on the given attachment ID.
.El
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm create
Create an attachment.
.Pp
The following flags can be specified:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s , -summary Ar summary
Summary of the attachment
.It Fl f , -file Ar path
Upload the given file as the attachment content.
You can also use
.Dq -
to read the content from stdin.
.It Fl i , -id Ar bug-id
Upload the attachment for the given
.Ar bug-id .
.It Fl F , -filename Ar filename
When uploading the file,
.Nm
uses the the filename from
.Fl f
to pass the filename to Bugzilla.
.Fl F
lets you pass a different file name and override the
.Fl f
provided name.
This is useful when reading the content from stdin.
.It Fl c , -comment Ar comment
Comment for the attachment.
.It Fl C , -content-type Ar content-type
Content type of the attachment.
This option is set automatically when
.Fl p
is set.
Otherwise this option is mandatory.
.It Fl p , -patch
The attachment is a patch.
When this flag is set you don't need to specify a content-type via
.Fl C .
.It Fl P , -private
The attachment is private.
.El
.El
.Sh ACTIONS
.Ar actions...
may be one or more of the following:
.Bl -tag -width "labels [options]"
.It Cm obsolete
Mark the attachment as obsolete.
.It Cm get Op Fl o Ar output
Print or download the attachment content.
When
.Fl o
is specified, the contents are written to the given file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print the content of attachment with ID 42:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gcli att -i 42 get
.Ed
.Pp
Create an attachment for bug 22 from a git diff:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git diff | gcli att create -f - -F gcli.diff -i 22 -s 'git diff' -p
.Ed
.Pp
Mark attachment 100 as obsolete:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gcli att -i 100 obsolete
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr gcli 1 ,
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Nico Sonack aka. herrhotzenplotz Aq Mt nsonack@herrhotzenplotz.de
and contributors.
.Sh BUGS
There are a lot of features missing in this subcommand.
